DIAG: ath12k: trace the four points inside srng_setup

Temporary, not for upstream.

Five rings are set up and the panic lands 41 ms after the fifth line
prints, before the sixth. The fifth is TCL_DATA(1); the sixth would be
its WBM2SW completion ring. Logging entry, allocation, and either side
of ath12k_hal_srng_setup() separates the possibilities: the fifth call
finishing and the sixth dying on entry, or the fifth dying inside
hal_srng_setup after its allocation succeeded.

The allocation numbers themselves check out -- every ring is
entries * entry_sz plus seven bytes of alignment, 0.78 MiB in total,
all of it below the Q6 reservations -- so this is not sizing or
exhaustion.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
@@ -246,6 +246,9 @@
 	int max_entries = ath12k_hal_srng_get_max_entries(ab, type);
 	int ret;
 
+	ath12k_warn(ab, "DBG: srng ENTER type=%d ring=%d req=%d max=%d esz=%d\n",
+		    type, ring_num, num_entries, max_entries, entry_sz);
+
 	if (max_entries < 0 || entry_sz < 0)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
@@ -260,6 +263,10 @@
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	ring->vaddr = PTR_ALIGN(ring->vaddr_unaligned, HAL_RING_BASE_ALIGN);
+
+	ath12k_warn(ab, "DBG: srng ALLOCED type=%d ring=%d entries=%d size=%d paddr=%pad\n",
+		    type, ring_num, num_entries, ring->size,
+		    &ring->paddr_unaligned);
 	ring->paddr = ring->paddr_unaligned + ((unsigned long)ring->vaddr -
 		      (unsigned long)ring->vaddr_unaligned);
 
@@ -326,7 +333,9 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	ath12k_warn(ab, "DBG: srng HAL_BEGIN type=%d ring=%d\n", type, ring_num);
 	ret = ath12k_hal_srng_setup(ab, type, ring_num, mac_id, &params);
+	ath12k_warn(ab, "DBG: srng HAL_DONE type=%d ring=%d ret=%d\n", type, ring_num, ret);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to setup srng: %d ring_id %d\n",
 			    ret, ring_num);
